  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An object &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&#39; is placed at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> in front of a concave mirror of radius of curvature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> as shown in the figure. The object starts moving towards the mirror at a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The position of the image from the mirror after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> will be at _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0100_9e01caf752a6.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 114px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "400",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>In&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, the object will travel distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>After <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sec</mi></math>, the object will be at distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.</p><p>Focal length of the concave mirror is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>200</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>Using mirror formula,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>u</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>80</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8000</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>Position of image from the mirror is at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}